!!! definition "Definition 123.11 : Pauli Matrices"
    Four extremely useful matrices are the **Pauli matrices**. These are $2 \times 2$ matrices and are commonly denoted by the equivalent notations below:

    $$
    \begin{aligned}
    \sigma_{0} \equiv I \equiv\left[\begin{array}{ll}
    1 & 0 \\
    0 & 1
    \end{array}\right] & \sigma_{1} \equiv \sigma_{x} \equiv X \equiv\left[\begin{array}{ll}
    0 & 1 \\
    1 & 0
    \end{array}\right] \\
    \sigma_{2} \equiv \sigma_{y} \equiv Y \equiv\left[\begin{array}{rr}
    0 & -i \\
    i & 0
    \end{array}\right] & \sigma_{3} \equiv \sigma_{z} \equiv Z \equiv\left[\begin{array}{rr}
    1 & 0 \\
    0 & -1
    \end{array}\right]
    \end{aligned}
    $$

