!!! theorem "Theorem 123.22 : Outer Product Representation of a Linear Operator"
    Let $A: V \rightarrow W$ be a linear operator, let $\{|v_i\rangle\}$ be an orthonormal basis for $V$, and let $\{|w_j\rangle\}$ be an orthonormal basis for $W$.
    Using **Theorem 2.1.21** (completeness relation) twice,

    $$
    \begin{equation*}
    A=I_W A I_V \tag{2.23}
    \end{equation*}
    $$

    $$
    \begin{align*}
    &=\sum_{ij}|w_j\rangle\langle w_j|A|v_i\rangle\langle v_i| \tag{2.24}\\
    &=\sum_{ij}\langle w_j|A|v_i\rangle\,|w_j\rangle\langle v_i|. \tag{2.25}
    \end{align*}
    $$

    Hence,

    $$
    A=\sum_{ij}\langle w_j|A|v_i\rangle\,|w_j\rangle\langle v_i|,
    $$

    which is the outer product representation of $A$.

